Design related IMPORTANT;
1. LOOK INTO THE FACT THAT YOUR BUFFER.H STORES VERTEX LAYOUT, WHEN IT SHOULD NOT DO THAT,
    YOUR MESH IS THE ONE THAT IS SUPPOSED TO BE DOING THAT, THEREFORE YOU HAVE TO MOVE ALL THE COUNTING TO THE MESH.H
    NOT IN BUFFER.H
2. I HAVE TO MAKE SURE THAT MY .OBJ READER THAT I WILL ADD IN THE FUTURE WILL INFER AND TELL TO MESH.H WHAT KIND
    OF ATTRIBUTES HAS TO BE SET, FOR EXAMPLE:
    while (read_line(file, line)) {
        if (line starts with "v ")  hasPositions = true;
        if (line starts with "vt ") hasUVs = true;
        if (line starts with "vn ") hasNormals = true;
    }

    if (hasPositions) add_mesh_attribute_layout(mesh, 3);
    if (hasNormals)   add_mesh_attribute_layout(mesh, 3);
    if (hasUVs)       add_mesh_attribute_layout(mesh, 2);

    AFTERWARDS APPLY THE REQUIRED SHADER BASED ON ATTRIBUTE TYPES OR MESH_TYPE IN MESH.H

